{"research_date": "2026-09-10", "pairs": [{"pair_id": "conflict_0e69b77d6c0aa193487dfce9", "claim_ids": ["claim_066610d6d05d3a62acbebe4f", "claim_250cdcd554dab0d700e6239e"], "query_ids": ["q_202"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_066610d6d05d3a62acbebe4f", "quote": "The Supreme Court of the United States has ruled 6-3 that tariffs imposed under the International Emergency Economic Powers Act (IEEPA) exceeded presidential authority.", "url": "https://www.shapiro.com/tariffs/tariff-news/current-tariffs", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"legal_authority": "International Emergency Economic Powers Act (IEEPA)"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_250cdcd554dab0d700e6239e", "quote": "On February 20, 2026, the Supreme Court ruled that IEEPA does not authorize the president to impose tariffs. The decision invalidated the April 2025 “Liberation Day” reciprocal tariffs, as well as the fentanyl-related tariffs imposed on imports from China, Mexico, and Canada.", "url": "https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/programs/geoeconomics-center/trump-tariff-tracker", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "IEEPA", "legal_authority": "International Emergency Economic Powers Act (IEEPA)", "reported_policy_status": "invalidated"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_cc3f75b0be49300ad6a814ab", "claim_ids": ["claim_28f461033b1950871fac3ae4", "claim_543555a92dfac25f9a498cb5"], "query_ids": ["q_204"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_28f461033b1950871fac3ae4", "quote": "Section 122 global surcharge | 10% | Expired — July 24, 2026 | No | Replaced IEEPA-based reciprocal tariffs effective February 24, 2026 at 12:01 a.m. EST. Applied to most imports. Certain categories excluded (USMCA-compliant goods, critical minerals, pharmaceuticals, electronics, passenger vehicles, aerospace). Expired July 24, 2026, when standard duties (MFN, Section 232, Section 301, etc.) — including the new Section 301 forced-labor tariff (10% or 12.5% by country of origin) — began applying to postal shipments for the first time.", "url": "https://zonos.com/docs/guides/us-tariff-changes", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "Section 122 global surcharge", "duty_rate": "10%", "effective_date": "February 24, 2026", "expiration_date": "July 24, 2026", "reported_policy_status": "Expired"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_543555a92dfac25f9a498cb5", "quote": "Announced – U.S. exempts electronics from reciprocal tariffs, pending sector-specific measures: The U.S. has temporarily excluded smartphones, laptops, and other consumer electronics from the 10% universal reciprocal tariff.", "url": "https://zonos.com/docs/guides/us-tariff-changes", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "reciprocal tariffs", "affected_product": "smartphones, laptops, and other consumer electronics", "duty_rate": "10%"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_fadfa57aaf70295a6bdaebc4", "claim_ids": ["claim_d6242ec9e801d72aaa1e25a2", "claim_e91ac6b0b65f0c3e7db9c1e4"], "query_ids": ["q_21"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_d6242ec9e801d72aaa1e25a2", "quote": "China faces a more unique situation. In January, President Trump imposed a 20 percent tariff on all goods from China. That means that a windshield wiper manufactured in China will face a 45 percent import tariff starting on May 3.", "url": "https://www.asashop.org/2025/04/04/understanding-the-new-tariffs-and-their-potential-impact-on-auto-repairers", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"country_of_origin": "China", "duty_rate": "45 percent", "effective_date": "May 3"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_e91ac6b0b65f0c3e7db9c1e4", "quote": "For example, the European Union will be subject to 20 percent tariffs, Thailand will be subject to a 36 percent rate, and China will be subject to a 34 percent levy. Providing an example for clarity, a tire produced in Thailand will only be subject to a 25 percent import tax.", "url": "https://www.asashop.org/2025/04/04/understanding-the-new-tariffs-and-their-potential-impact-on-auto-repairers", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"country_of_origin": "Thailand", "duty_rate": "25 percent", "announcement_date": "April 2"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_8971909c331290f7b68a5472", "claim_ids": ["claim_403462270e5cdb8a13f131ef", "claim_47112914e93f90cbbe933651"], "query_ids": ["q_210"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_403462270e5cdb8a13f131ef", "quote": "Any exclusion will be effective starting from the date of publication of the exclusion determination in the Federal Register and will extend through May 31, 2025.", "url": "https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2024/10/17/2024-23880/procedures-for-requests-to-exclude-certain-machinery-used-in-domestic-manufacturing-from-actions", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "official_trade_authority", "fields": {"tariff_program": "Section 301", "expiration_date": "May 31, 2025"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_47112914e93f90cbbe933651", "quote": "the docket for submitting exclusions opens on October 15, 2024. The deadline for submitting exclusion requests is March 31, 2025.", "url": "https://ustr.gov/about-us/policy-offices/press-office/press-releases/2024/october/ustr-opens-exclusion-process-certain-machinery-used-domestic-manufacturing", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "official_trade_authority", "fields": {"announcement_date": "October 15, 2024", "expiration_date": "March 31, 2025"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_4407f6161b3870420d3cb337", "claim_ids": ["claim_403462270e5cdb8a13f131ef", "claim_ba16d5bae81f41a41fc0e9cc"], "query_ids": ["q_210"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_403462270e5cdb8a13f131ef", "quote": "Any exclusion will be effective starting from the date of publication of the exclusion determination in the Federal Register and will extend through May 31, 2025.", "url": "https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2024/10/17/2024-23880/procedures-for-requests-to-exclude-certain-machinery-used-in-domestic-manufacturing-from-actions", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "official_trade_authority", "fields": {"tariff_program": "Section 301", "expiration_date": "May 31, 2025"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_ba16d5bae81f41a41fc0e9cc", "quote": "Exclusions granted will be effective upon publication in the Federal Register and valid through May 31, 2025.", "url": "https://www.hklaw.com/en/insights/publications/2024/12/continuing-trend-section-301-machinery-exclusion", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"expiration_date": "May 31, 2025"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_e01972f481b4cbdc88298f73", "claim_ids": ["claim_47112914e93f90cbbe933651", "claim_5fbead0f36a89a07fded9c90"], "query_ids": ["q_210"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_47112914e93f90cbbe933651", "quote": "the docket for submitting exclusions opens on October 15, 2024. The deadline for submitting exclusion requests is March 31, 2025.", "url": "https://ustr.gov/about-us/policy-offices/press-office/press-releases/2024/october/ustr-opens-exclusion-process-certain-machinery-used-domestic-manufacturing", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "official_trade_authority", "fields": {"announcement_date": "October 15, 2024", "expiration_date": "March 31, 2025"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_5fbead0f36a89a07fded9c90", "quote": "Any exclusion will be effective starting from the date of publication of the exclusion determination in the Federal Register and will extend through May 31, 2025.", "url": "https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2024/10/17/2024-23880/procedures-for-requests-to-exclude-certain-machinery-used-in-domestic-manufacturing-from-actions", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "official_trade_authority", "fields": {"effective_date": "date of publication of the exclusion determination in the Federal Register", "expiration_date": "May 31, 2025"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_7843620334e430f7a3c9d2be", "claim_ids": ["claim_039794f0b09de89383719235", "claim_a973f21d553542cb1cddb2ee"], "query_ids": ["q_211"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_039794f0b09de89383719235", "quote": "Finally, the U.S. Trade Representative proposed 19 temporary exclusions for solar manufacturing equipment.", "url": "https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2024/09/18/2024-21217/notice-of-modification-chinas-acts-policies-and-practices-related-to-technology-transfer", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "official_trade_authority", "fields": {"tariff_program": "section 301 tariffs"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_a973f21d553542cb1cddb2ee", "quote": "In response to the President's direction, the U.S. Trade Representative proposed 312 subheadings eligible for consideration of temporary exclusion, and proposed 19 temporary exclusions for solar manufacturing equipment.", "url": "https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2024/09/18/2024-21217/notice-of-modification-chinas-acts-policies-and-practices-related-to-technology-transfer", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "official_trade_authority", "fields": {}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_8fe926d53dff81fd596cf94c", "claim_ids": ["claim_3cc17b0347eba3a1d9f1cfc1", "claim_8ac6fae45d2f50818344facb"], "query_ids": ["q_211"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_3cc17b0347eba3a1d9f1cfc1", "quote": "On September 13, 2024, USTR announced it had granted 14 tariff exclusions for specific solar manufacturing equipment, effective from Jan. 1, 2024, through May 31, 2025.", "url": "https://www.strtrade.com/trade-news-resources/tariff-actions-resources/section-301-tariffs-on-china", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"affected_product": "solar manufacturing equipment", "effective_date": "Jan. 1, 2024", "expiration_date": "May 31, 2025", "reported_policy_status": "granted"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_8ac6fae45d2f50818344facb", "quote": "the U.S. Trade Representative has determined not to adopt the five exclusions covering solar manufacturing equipment for modules.", "url": "https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2024/09/18/2024-21217/notice-of-modification-chinas-acts-policies-and-practices-related-to-technology-transfer", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "official_trade_authority", "fields": {}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_85fb8b275787df277606b3c3", "claim_ids": ["claim_09a379c12ef29e7791d39999", "claim_12bd65580741739c2b5c8bb0"], "query_ids": ["q_213"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_09a379c12ef29e7791d39999", "quote": "It was determined that a substantial transformation occurred, and further, the critical components to making an electric vehicle – battery pack,", "url": "https://rulings.cbp.gov/ruling/H155115", "kind": "search_snippet", "publisher_type": "official_trade_authority", "fields": {}}, {"claim_id": "claim_12bd65580741739c2b5c8bb0", "quote": "CBP has previously held that assembling battery cells into battery packs does not characterize substantial transformation of the battery cells because the fundamental character of the cells is not altered simply by being placed together in plastic casing. See HQ 563045 (Aug. 9, 2004) and HQ 734393 (Mar. 20, 1992).", "url": "https://www.cmtradelaw.com/2023/01/customs-ruling-of-the-week-country-of-origin-of-battery-modules-and-battery-packs-and-the-applicability-of-certain-trade-remedies-under-section-301", "kind": "search_snippet", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_0c11224fb54e0f6e3b1b7667", "claim_ids": ["claim_12bd65580741739c2b5c8bb0", "claim_399142074bc05e0764b3471a"], "query_ids": ["q_213"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_12bd65580741739c2b5c8bb0", "quote": "CBP has previously held that assembling battery cells into battery packs does not characterize substantial transformation of the battery cells because the fundamental character of the cells is not altered simply by being placed together in plastic casing. See HQ 563045 (Aug. 9, 2004) and HQ 734393 (Mar. 20, 1992).", "url": "https://www.cmtradelaw.com/2023/01/customs-ruling-of-the-week-country-of-origin-of-battery-modules-and-battery-packs-and-the-applicability-of-certain-trade-remedies-under-section-301", "kind": "search_snippet", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {}}, {"claim_id": "claim_399142074bc05e0764b3471a", "quote": "the assembly of the glider and other components of various origins constitutes a substantial transformation and results in an article with a new name, character, and use, such that the country of origin for the TCE vehicle is the U.S. for purposes of U.S. Government procurement.", "url": "https://rulings.cbp.gov/ruling/H155115", "kind": "search_snippet", "publisher_type": "official_trade_authority", "fields": {"country_of_origin": "the U.S."}}]}]}

